{
  "id": "crt-scanline-damage",
  "name": "CRT Scanline Damage",
  "url": "shaders/crt-scanline-damage.wgsl",
  "description": "Damaged CRT monitor simulation with depth-aware barrel distortion, RGB phosphor triad mask, a real raster of scanlines, flicker, temporal phosphor decay via dataTextureC, treble snow and scar rows, occasional dark-band fault, and click degauss rings. Upgraded with a misconvergence swirl (degauss rings pull the R/G/B rasters apart radially with a rotating magenta/green purity blotch that settles), flyback retrace lines during the dark-band fault, and a radial chromatic barrel (the RGB split grows toward the tube edges).",
  "tags": [
    "crt",
    "scanline",
    "retro",
    "distortion",
    "glitch",
    "phosphor",
